-- title:
--   Hecke eigenplane in the Tate module of J₀(N)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $N \ge 1$, and $S$ a finite set of natural numbers with $p \in S$. Let $\mathcal{O}'$ be a complete (adically complete for its maximal ideal) discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field, with $p$ in its maximal ideal, and let $\chi$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$) and $U_q$ ($q \mid N$ prime, $q \notin S$) — to $\mathcal{O}'$. The assertion is that there is a discrete valuation domain $\mathcal{O}''$ with the same properties (domain, discrete valuation, adic completeness, finite residue field, characteristic zero), equipped with an $\mathcal{O}'$-algebra structure making it module-finite over $\mathcal{O}'$ by an injective local homomorphism, and with a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra structure, such that for every fraction field $K$ of $\mathcal{O}''$ the following holds. Write $T =$ [`ModularCurve.TateModule p (ModularCurve.JZero N)`](def/ModularCurve_EichlerShimuraData.html#L15) for the submodule of sequences $x : \mathbb{N} \to J$ with $x_0 = 0$ and $p \cdot x_{n+1} = x_n$, where $J = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the modular function field of level $N$ base-changed to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, carrying the module structure over $\mathrm{HeckeAlg} = \mathbb{Z}[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ given by [`ModularCurve.heckeModuleBar N`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeModule.html#L82). Suppose given: a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-module structure on $T$ whose scalar action is computed componentwise through the reductions $\mathbb{Z}_p \to \mathbb{Z}/p^n$; a monoid homomorphism $\rho_M$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ (as $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphisms over $\mathbb{Q}$) to $\mathcal{O}''$-endomorphisms of $\mathcal{O}'' \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} T$ which on pure tensors $a \otimes x$ returns $a \otimes y$ whenever $y$ is the componentwise translate $\sigma \cdot x$; and a ring homomorphism $TM$ from $\mathrm{HeckeAlg}$ to the same endomorphism ring with $TM(t)(a \otimes x) = a \otimes (t \cdot x)$. Then $K \otimes_{\mathcal{O}''} (\mathcal{O}'' \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p} T)$ contains a $K$-submodule $W$ of rank $2$, stable under the base change to $K$ of every $\rho_M(\sigma)$, such that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$ the base change of $TM(X_\ell)$ acts on $W$ as multiplication by the image of $\chi(T_\ell)$ in $K$, and for every such $\ell$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$ and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ and acting on the residue field of $A$ by $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$, the trace on $W$ of the restriction of the base change of $\rho_M(\sigma)$ equals the image of $\chi(T_\ell)$ in $K$.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura construction in the form attached to a single point of the weight-two Hecke algebra: the $p$-adic representation cut out on the Tate module of $J_0(N)$ by a character $\chi$, after allowing a finite extension of the coefficient ring. It is used by the corresponding statement for newforms, by the local flatness assertion at $p$, and by the irreducibility input to level lowering.
